WEBVTT

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:05.400
Rice and a normal meal is where it's at!

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.000
That's right. If Mr. Kurokawa were here,

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.640
we'd get fed noodles for breakfast and lunch.

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:10.640
<i>The Wide show Special
Hamdara's Great Treasure
Closing in on its
allure and mysteries</i>

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:13.980
The royal mummy excavated
in the Hamdara Kingdom

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.380
two years ago attracted a great deal of attention,

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:19.720
and it has been decided that the Diamond Eyes
mummy, which is its nickname,

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:20.940
will be on display in Japan.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.650
The topic of interest is
the reason behind that name.

00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.590
That is the gigantic diamonds
wedged into its eye sockets,

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:29.790
which are believed to be more than
one thousand carats.

00:00:29.990 --> 00:00:32.860
All of its teeth have also been
replaced with diamonds,

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.890
and its value is immeasurable.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.270
Diamond eyes and diamond crowns?

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:42.070
Looking at someone's dried-up
old body is boring.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:43.410
It's not edible.

00:00:42.970 --> 00:00:55.480
<i>The Wide show
Special!
Hamdara's Great Treasure!</i>

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:47.040
But this mummy seems to have
an odd rumor circulating around it.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.080
It seems that those who participated
in its excavation

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.880
are dying under strange circumstances.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.710
Yes, the people of Hamdara are afraid
this might be the mummy's curse.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:59.580
A curse, they say. Sounds interesting!

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.260
That kind of rumor is purposely spread
to discourage thieves.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.560
There's no way there's a curse.

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.960
Well, yeah. It's just a dried-up old body.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.110
<i>Norikonda sabaibaru cousutaa</i>

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.080
The survival roller coaster we got on

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.850
There's no need to give up,
run by the highway

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.550
<i>Akirame muyoude run by the highway</i>

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:23.420
<i>Kimiwa inochi karagara</i>

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:23.620
You just barely escaped with your life

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.950
<i>Atashitachimo nodoga karakara</i>

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:26.220
We're thirsty

00:01:25.950 --> 00:01:28.150
<i>Kyokugento mugendai</i>

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.360
Extremities and infinity

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:30.490
<i>Tomo ni sorette mugendai</i>

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.720
Together, they form a fantasy

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.390
<i>Kamaeta me hibana chiri</i>

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.590
The eyes, squaring away, are
throwing out sparks

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:35.420
<i>Oni-san kochira to shita o dasu</i>

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:35.650
"You're it! This way, " you say,
as you stick your tongue out

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:37.650
<i>Wink</i>

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:37.720
Wink

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:41.330
<i>Kyouretsuna itamini kansha</i>

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.540
Grateful for the excruciating pain

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.670
<i>Power to iu na no rei de henkan</i>

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.970
I'm restored by a gratitude
known as power

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:49.580
<i>Mou sorosoro okaeri asobareta houga
iinodewa naide shouka</i>

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:49.780
Perhaps it would be better too return soon?

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:58.480
<i>Matsugeno sukima umeruyouni aimeiku</i>

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:58.720
As though filling in the gaps between
the eyelashes, eye make

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:05.790
<i>Kokorono sukima umeruyouni I take</i>

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:05.990
As though filling in the gaps of
my heart, I take

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:10.260
<i>Gekiretsu panchide gyakuni takamaru</i>

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:10.460
On the contrary, the intensity is heightened
by a powerful punch

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:14.730
<i>Yabai shiuchi hodo yokei moechauwa</i>

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:14.800
The worse I'm treated, the more I get fired up

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:19.100
<i>Mouretsu panchide atashi takaburu</i>

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:19.240
I get worked up over an intense punch

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:27.530
<i>Sonna koto shite kurete arigatou</i>

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:28.080
Thank you for doing such a thing

00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:30.050
<i>Sukima sukima sukimani mimai</i>

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:30.250
A gap, a gap, pay a sympathy visit

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:32.050
<i>Janai janai itainjanai?</i>

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:32.220
Doesn't it, doesn't it, doesn't it hurt?

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:33.720
<i>Mimai tsurai? ltai? Yabai?</i>

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.990
Is the visit painful? Does it hurt?
Is it dangerous?

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:38.350
<i>lkitai itai shitai, lkitai itai shitai</i>

00:02:33.990 --> 00:02:38.660
I want to go, I want to stay, I want to do it

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:47.700
<i>Shell of the Cursed</i>

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:50.890
I'm Furahre Nabacola, of the Nation
of Hamdala's Security Agency.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:55.460
Hamdala... You mean the one with the mummy?

00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:00.710
I've come regarding the Diamond Eyes mummy.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:01.730
Eye?

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:03.910
Courier?

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:08.720
Even though we're poor,
courier duty isn't our job.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:13.520
Not to mention the other time we got into
a pickle transporting that germ, right?

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:17.320
That's right. Why did you accept that job?

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:24.760
Well, Mr. Pointy-head, this job is truly
for a danger service agency.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:31.310
The job is simple. It's to transport
the Diamond Eyes mummy.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.140
What the?

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:35.710
That kind of great treasure...

00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:39.200
Why are you asking us to do this?

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:42.720
It's the curse.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:44.180
The curse?

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:46.410
The curse.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.290
So that's it.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:56.330
The mummy to be transported has
a spectacularly effective curse placed on it.

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:59.000
Spectacular, you say...

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.100
It wasn't our intention to let it
leak to the mass media,

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:04.040
but the staff who investigated it,

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.510
the workers who transported it from the grave,

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:10.700
without exception, it's the truth that anyone
involved with it has died mysteriously.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:15.150
Japanese transporters didn't want to
handle that sort of thing,

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:17.650
so they rejected us.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.720
What does this all mean?

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:22.050
You want us to take on the curse instead?

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.660
Starting here in Japan,

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:29.560
we plan to have exhibits in sixteen countries
around the world.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:33.000
To a poor nation such as ours,

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.940
the world exhibit of the Diamond Eyes mummy
is an indispensable source of income.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:44.170
Should something disastrous happen in Japan,
the place of the first exhibit...

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:48.180
Your provincial tour plans go down the drain.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:55.480
We've arranged for the transportation of the
other treasures through normal channels.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:59.290
That's why with the Diamond Eyes mummy,
taking a different route...

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.030
With us, even if something were to happen,

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:05.990
the media won't get a lead on us and
anything could be erased, like using an eraser.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:08.060
That is correct.

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:11.540
How brutally blunt you are.

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:19.140
I'm not good dealing with curses, ghosts, aliens,
and blonde, tight-bodied pheromone wives.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:21.880
Say, how many digits are on there?

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:26.590
So we're supposed to carry the curse.

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:30.490
But man, how do we end up with
all these ridiculous assignments?!

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:34.000
For an ordinary transportation job,
the money is exceptional.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.790
Oh, wow! You're right!

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:40.330
This is like, we're going to challenge
the mummy's curse!

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:44.370
Like, could you lay off saying things
that might be damning to us?

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:47.210
Inside, I'm actually pretty frightened.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:51.280
Then why did you take the contract for this job?

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.180
Necessity knows no law.

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:57.550
Just the operational expenses of the agency
alone are putting us in the red.

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:01.960
There's no stronger argument
than saying we're poor.

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:05.090
Let's do it, let's do it, let's go do it!

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:08.060
That's right. That's the case.
Let go get exorcised.
Let's do it, let's do it, let's go do it!

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:10.830
<i>Mugi-ya</i>

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:21.980
Thanks for the business!

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.000
Thank you yourself.

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:28.980
At that hour, the congestion
on the highway is very bad.

00:06:28.980 --> 00:06:30.350
I see.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:33.350
All the routes are kind of iffy.

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:37.450
To think, we're the ones to carry such
an extremely important cultural object...

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:40.300
On the contrary, it's good we're
the ones doing the job.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:41.900
Yeah, you're right. That's the case.

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:43.200
If someone is carelessly exhibitionistic,

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:45.530
some unscrupulous goons will start taking aim.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:53.580
Anyway, the diamonds are worth
dozens of millions of dollars.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.200
I don't think there's anyone who
wants the mummy.

00:06:59.050 --> 00:06:59.910
Pops!

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:03.950
Ow... ow...

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.720
My stomach hurts...

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:16.500
Have the job finished within the week.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.000
Sure.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:20.430
There's no turning back now.

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:30.940
Pops, get a hold of yourself.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.210
I'm done for.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:45.990
It's unusual for Pops to get food poisoning
from udon noodles.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:48.600
So it really is the mummy's curse.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:52.330
No way. Anyway, I'll head to the hospital.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:53.230
Sure.

00:07:56.270 --> 00:07:57.300
Take care!

00:08:02.740 --> 00:08:04.080
That person...

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.810
A curse? There's no such...

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:14.550
It's not working!

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:15.320
<i>Wives Club
Welcome
All you can drink,
all you can sing
90 minutes for 5000 yen</i>

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:31.710
Am I just holding you guys back?

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:33.510
That's not true.

00:08:33.510 --> 00:08:37.080
Like when it comes to computers,
we're always relying on you and Harada.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:40.080
But with the kind of jobs we do,
if something were to happen,

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:42.570
wouldn't your family worry?

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.750
Like they would worry.

00:08:45.390 --> 00:08:46.440
Asami...

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:51.080
I want to become strong. Like you, Miss Mikura!

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:56.990
If you're of a weak heart, you won't
live long enough to eat dinner. Got it?

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:58.990
Right.

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:02.640
This time, we'll be sufficient for the job.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:05.170
All we're doing is transporting
one big dried-up body.

00:09:05.170 --> 00:09:08.210
But maybe you shouldn't say things like that.

00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:10.440
There is the example of Mr. Kurokawa.

00:09:11.810 --> 00:09:14.110
Just because Pops got a stomachache...

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:16.550
Asami!

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:25.350
Miss Mikura, that was...

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:31.290
And it was only last week that
I sent it out for maintenance.

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:34.370
But I'm glad you're safe.

00:09:34.370 --> 00:09:36.300
Even Mikura and the rest of you...

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:39.600
Maybe we should cancel after all?

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.300
It's coincidence. Coincidence.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:46.840
It's about the fox-style udon noodles
from yesterday...

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:49.010
Isn't that your usual?

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:51.650
<i>Grand Opening
All noodles, half off</i>

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:54.120
Yesterday, I saw a flier for a new
noodle shop's half price sale.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:57.830
It happened because you ordered
those half-off noodles.

00:09:57.830 --> 00:10:01.260
Me getting food poisoning from
udon noodles is an embarrassment.

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:03.330
I thought about putting in a claim
and filing for damages,

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:06.600
then putting it out of business,
or so I thought, but...

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.060
There wasn't anything.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:14.680
No such udon noodle shop.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.140
That means...

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:17.510
That's ridiculous.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:19.810
As soon as we accepted the job,
something like this happened.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:22.910
I think I understand what he meant
by a spectacularly effective curse.

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:25.120
Let's do it!

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:28.560
You're just something dried-up,
so don't take us live bodies so lightly!

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:31.550
So let's stop taking that defiant sort of attitude.

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:35.490
Miss Mikura, you shouldn't be so provoking.

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.200
Mr. Harada...

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:42.760
Well, whatever the case, we can't cancel.

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:47.270
We don't have the money to pay
the breach of contract penalty.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:50.680
Right.

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:17.930
All right! Let absolutely nothing go through!

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:20.410
From the Nation of Hamlada's charter jet,

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:24.280
containers with all sorts of treasures
are being unloaded.

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:30.410
Does the greatest treasure in the world, the
Diamond Eyes mummy, lie among one of them?

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:38.920
Hey, wait! Where's that container going?!

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:42.730
It's all right. That one's going
on a separate vehicle.

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:44.800
Separate vehicle?

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:46.500
I haven't heard anything about that.

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:48.660
There was a sudden change in the plan.

00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:01.410
Okay, that should do it.

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:03.880
The dried-up old body's bed is complete!

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:08.420
The police don't suspect a thing

00:12:08.420 --> 00:12:11.790
and are carrying a dummy mummy
with the other treasures.

00:12:12.130 --> 00:12:16.220
I've made arrangements with the museum,
so you can go in as is.

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:18.720
This is quite heavy.

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:21.970
Carry it carefully, pointy-hair.

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:24.770
Pops! I'm ready over here!

00:12:24.770 --> 00:12:27.370
You haven't pulled a prank, have you, Mikura?

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:29.610
What's this?

00:12:29.610 --> 00:12:32.250
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:33.680
Mr. Kurokawa!

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.120
This is disastrous! Oh, my! Oh, my!

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:38.350
What have you done?!

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:40.320
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:12:44.730 --> 00:12:46.490
It looks like it's all right.

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:48.500
I think my life span just shrank a little,
like cheap underwear after a wash.

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:51.400
Oh, thank God, thank God.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:54.440
Wow, he's got all sorts of decorations
all over his body.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:56.100
No wonder he's heavy.

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:01.800
What was that just now?

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:07.250
Why?

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.450
It's the curse!

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:13.040
For real?

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:17.250
Anyway, I'll immediately arrange
for another vehicle.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:19.630
We're going to continue?

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:23.430
Hey, dried-up potato! Give it a rest already!

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:25.830
Don't break it, I'm begging you, please stop!

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:27.740
Take that! And that! Say something!

00:13:27.440 --> 00:13:31.170
Please stop! My magistrate! My Lady Mikura!
My Lord and Master Mikura!

00:13:28.900 --> 00:13:31.400
Pisses me off! Take that!

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:35.180
Damn, lucky bastards.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:55.730
It's going a bit out of the way, but
it's great the road's pretty clear.

00:13:55.730 --> 00:13:59.600
Yeah, one, please let us be safe.
Two, let us arrive that way.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.200
So you say...

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:08.980
Mikura, I hope you haven't done anything
to incur a curse from the mummy.

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:11.650
Well, maybe she's doing something already.

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:13.080
Why?!

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:16.220
She said something about wanting
to lecture the mummy.

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:18.950
Lecture?! Oh, my God! So disappointed!

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:24.890
Say, you, we're trying to deliver you
to where you belong.

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:26.730
Why are you interfering?

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:30.990
If that's the way you feel, I'll just sell you
to a dry foods store, as is.

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:36.300
Please, let Mikura not have said
anything rude to Mr. Mummy.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:38.730
Hey, Mr. Kurokawa...

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:41.900
What, there's something else?! What now?!

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:46.840
Behind us.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.610
How conspicuous.

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:54.050
Mikura, be careful. A suspicious car's...

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:55.750
What?

00:14:59.030 --> 00:15:00.650
Whoa, whoa, whoa, wait a minute!

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:09.790
Damn!

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:11.900
Ow...

00:15:13.940 --> 00:15:15.570
What are you doing?!

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:20.480
Whoa, wait a minute, no!

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:26.520
Oh, man...

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:47.000
I'm not afraid of the living.
They're as harmless as a young goat in a forest.

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:53.510
Harada, there are three more cars! Lose them!

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:57.640
We have more horsepower,
but speed is another matter!

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:05.710
Damn.

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:12.560
It's all right. I'll protect you. It's my job.

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:19.470
Damn!

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:25.250
Two down!

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:28.380
Is Mr. Mummy all right, Mummy,
I mean, Mikura?

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:31.110
Mikura, can you hear me? Mikura?

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:42.790
Oh, hell!

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:55.700
Come out with your hands up!

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:58.150
Oh, boy...

00:16:58.150 --> 00:16:59.710
Open up the truck's cargo bay.

00:16:59.710 --> 00:17:01.550
Who the hell are you guys? Tell me.

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:03.140
Hurry it up!

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:04.650
Harada!

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:05.520
Okay!

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:10.850
Mikura...

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:13.760
Stay very hidden, Mikura.

00:17:14.330 --> 00:17:16.920
It's settled. Come immediately.

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:24.960
It looks like she's hiding very well.

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:31.510
But this is so unlike her.
Usually she opens fire immediately.

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:33.850
I wonder if she's injured?

00:17:37.490 --> 00:17:39.820
Now, you guys need to die.

00:17:40.760 --> 00:17:44.190
By the way, you guys will be cursed
by Mr. Mummy too.

00:17:47.030 --> 00:17:49.360
Cursed? So he said.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:56.040
The one setting up the curse wasn't
Diamond Eyes, but us.

00:17:56.040 --> 00:17:57.440
What do you mean?

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:03.340
It's a bit difficult to nab treasure guarded
by the military within Hamdala's borders.

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:05.880
The plan was to take advantage
of the curse rumor,

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:08.620
and while the Japanese workers
had second thoughts,

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:11.590
our transportation crew was
supposed to go after them.

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:15.080
However, we discovered that the mummy
was going to be transported by you guys.

00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:18.560
Well, it's not like we didn't give you
enough warnings.

00:18:18.560 --> 00:18:21.000
I see. It wasn't the curse.

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:23.700
Had you guys obediently gotten off this case,

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:26.760
we wouldn't have had to go this far either.

00:18:28.770 --> 00:18:30.130
Hey, open it!

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:37.140
We tried threatening you,
but you guys never responded.

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:39.110
Then what we went through all that time was...

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:40.780
The fox-style udon noodles!

00:18:40.780 --> 00:18:44.350
Had you obediently canceled the job...

00:18:44.350 --> 00:18:46.150
We're the Danger Service Agency.

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:49.160
We didn't believe in the curse in the first place.

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:50.220
Mr. Kurokawa?

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:54.460
That's what I thought.
That's why we decided to use force.

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:59.030
What we wanted to do was to blow the truck up
and get rid of you in an instant,

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:01.470
but you guys have persistently good luck.

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:21.150
Mikura!

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:25.580
You need to take care of people
of the past, right?

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:39.300
Mikura, how?

00:19:40.010 --> 00:19:44.880
I knew someone was targeting us.
The mummy told me.

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:47.080
Mr. Mummy did?

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:53.410
Yeah, when the car started to go wild,
I got the idea of trading places with him.

00:19:57.260 --> 00:19:58.620
I'll borrow this for a moment.

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:01.630
Well, when someone deserving of
being cursed comes this far,

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.630
maybe Mr. Mummy will have it
in his heart to forgive.

00:20:03.630 --> 00:20:06.700
Rather than that, wearing a mummy's clothes...

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:09.360
Isn't that usually disgusting?!

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:13.830
Damn...

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:17.470
Die!

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:23.020
My arm! My arm!

00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:25.410
What?

00:20:35.660 --> 00:20:37.560
All right, it ended safely.

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:39.690
Chief!

00:20:41.370 --> 00:20:44.000
The mummy... the Diamond Eyes mummy!

00:20:44.000 --> 00:20:44.970
What?

00:20:46.610 --> 00:20:48.300
This is...

00:20:52.680 --> 00:20:54.200
What's the meaning of this?!

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:56.240
My apologies.

00:20:57.380 --> 00:21:01.190
Due to circumstances within my office,
we requested a third party for the job.

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:03.590
A third party? Who?

00:21:03.590 --> 00:21:07.420
Please relax. They have arrived safely as well.

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:13.670
All right! All right! All right! All right! All right!

00:21:14.800 --> 00:21:16.000
They're...

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.970
Thank you for a job well done.

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:19.070
Kurokawa!

00:21:19.070 --> 00:21:23.840
Who cares whether they're rocks or a mummy?
We both completed our jobs.

00:21:23.840 --> 00:21:24.830
See you later.

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:29.410
Why the hell do these guys...

00:21:29.850 --> 00:21:31.320
I can't wait any longer!

00:21:34.690 --> 00:21:38.090
You didn't show up for a while,
so I was worried.

00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:40.160
So that's what happened.

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:43.100
By the way, when the truck exploded...

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:47.940
You and Pops stumbled
and dropped the mummy.

00:21:47.940 --> 00:21:50.640
That's why I was saved.

00:21:50.640 --> 00:21:53.070
Just like when the gun exploded.

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:57.170
It's a coincidence, coincidence.

00:21:58.010 --> 00:22:00.780
Sorry I called you a dried potato.

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:05.520
Rain...

00:22:05.520 --> 00:22:08.820
Oh, no! If he gets wet,
he'll turn back the way he was!

00:22:08.820 --> 00:22:10.120
We'd better move him quick!

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:15.220
He's not dried seaweed,
so if he comes back the way he was...

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:19.000
We're the ones who are free to go back.

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:20.860
The rest will be taken care of by the people here.

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:22.870
Well, then.

00:22:22.870 --> 00:22:23.960
Let's go home!

00:22:28.910 --> 00:22:31.280
I have to hand it to you, Asami.
You come prepared.

00:22:31.610 --> 00:22:34.240
I'm sorry it's so small.

00:22:36.480 --> 00:22:38.250
This is nothing.

00:22:39.450 --> 00:22:41.890
Right, right. They do say idiots
never catch a cold.

00:22:41.890 --> 00:22:44.290
Hey, wait a minute. Who are you talking about?

00:22:43.720 --> 00:22:47.160
One, two, three. I wonder when the rest of
the money will be transferred to the bank?

00:22:47.160 --> 00:22:49.260
First, repair the Beetle.

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:52.930
Then, listen to the Beatles.
Hey, Jude. Yeah, right.

00:22:52.930 --> 00:22:55.900
Serves you right. What? Am I weird?

00:22:59.570 --> 00:23:01.970
Hey, wait for me. Give me money too.
This always happens.

